//? Title: Feature visualization:all channels and explicit regularized tensor ascent
//? Requires: vanilla_saliency.mepml
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
An internal convolutional channel can prefer patterns that are hard to identify from its weights. Optimize explicit synthetic inputs for every frozen MNISTconv2channel,show every TensorSGD step and image prior,and retain all channels and control outcomes.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.11_interpretability/feature_visualization.cpp`.

> The method

For selected post-ReLUchannelc,maximize its spatial mean while explicitly penalizing centered pixel energy and squared neighbor differences:

$$ J_c(x)=mean(A_c(x))-\lambda mean((x-.5)^2)-\tau[mean((\Delta_yx)^2)+mean((\Delta_xx)^2)]. $$
\alttext(The selected-channel mean response subtracts a centered mean-square image prior and separately normalized vertical and horizontal squared-difference penalties.)

Plain tensorSGD on the negative RMS-normalized ordinary derivative proposes bounded image changes;actual complete-objective backtracking accepts nondecreases. Model parameters remain frozen. Uniformnoise initialization is declared synthetic;this is channel-preference synthesis rather than attribution to a real observation.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/feature_visualization_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/feature_visualization_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/feature_visualization_concept.tikz > build/feature_visualization_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/feature_visualization_concept.svg build/feature_visualization_concept.dvi > build/feature_visualization_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
