\caption(Feature visualization:all channels and explicit regularized tensor ascent)
\alttext(Explicit synthetic;  uniform starts; then Selected feature;  and visible priors; then Visible TensorSGD;  all channels and controls.)

> The optimized input is explicit synthetic noise

Restore the exact frozen MNIST classifier and actual initial arrays from
[vanilla saliency](vanilla_saliency.mepml),where all96tensor Adam fitting
updates and held-out errors are visible. There is no new classifier fitting.
Here the inputs are deliberately SYNTHETICuniform noise,not real MNIST images:
16independent28pxstarts,one per selected conv2channel0..15. Seeds1423and1429
are fixed before inspecting results. Every channel is retained without selection
by its response or visual appearance.

The objective for one selected channel is its mean spatial post-ReLUresponse,
minus.01times mean(x-.5)^2and.2times squared-TV. Squared-TV is the sum of
mean squared vertical and horizontal first differences,not absolute TV.
The three objective terms remain visible. Maximizing one channel does not
suppress every other channel and need not produce a digit or semantic prototype.

> Executed tensor architecture

The diagram shows the forward MNIST CNN that the attribution or feature-optimization method inspects; the attribution algorithm is explained separately.

This figure executes the inference configuration shown in the code, using a zero-valued
shape probe without fitting or loading a checkpoint. Named stage boundaries group
whole subgraphs where available; other nodes retain functional-layer detail. Exact
batch-inclusive shapes and reachable parameter totals come from the trace. Shared
linear scales map spatial dimensions and channel counts to blocks; the one-pixel
visibility floor is disclosed in the legend. Labels use compact monospace text,
rotate counterclockwise and sit beside their own glyphs. Arrows flow left to right;
wide diagrams scroll at native size on the website.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/feature_visualization_architecture.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  n::set_num_threads(2);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  n::ParameterStore p(1103);
  n::Module         architecture_model(
      [&](const n::Tensor& image) { return m::SaliencyCnn(p, image).logits; },
      "Feature visualization:all channels and explicit regularized tensor ascent");
  n::ModelPlotOptions options;
  options.style                 = n::ModelPlotStyle::Flow;
  options.detail                = n::ModelPlotDetail::Blocks;
  options.labels                = {.type = n::ModelPlotLabel::NameAndShape, .size = 12, .wrap = 24};
  options.spacing               = {.layer = 24, .lane = 12, .label = 8, .margin = 20};
  options.sizing.spatial_size   = 96;
  options.sizing.channel_size   = 42;
  options.sizing.minimum_extent = 1;
  options.opacity               = .8;
  const auto diagram            = architecture_model.plot(n::zeros({1, 28, 28, 1}), options);
  diagram.save_svg("build/feature_visualization_architecture.svg");
  std::print(
      "{} displayed nodes; {} reachable learned values.\n",
      diagram.nodes().size(),
      diagram.parameter_count());
}
```
