> Exact image-prior derivatives and actual noise starts

A declared feature map[image,2*image]and selected channel1give a2*xspatial
mean. Native independent checks verify the full objective,all784image gradients
and all1512squared-TVedges including boundaries. The batchmean derivative has
an explicit1/Bfactor. Uniform inputs use raw mt19937draws and Doubletensor
(raw+.5)/2^32scaling beforeFloat32rounding,with exact seeded replay.
```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/feature_visualization_noise.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  const auto first = m::FeatureNoise(16, 1423), second = m::FeatureNoise(16, 1429);
  const auto x = m::FeatureNoise(1, 1433).requires_grad_();
  const auto objective = m::VisualizeFeature(x, n::concat({x, x * 2.}, 3),
                                             n::ones({1}, n::DType::Int32), 2, .3f, .7f);
  const auto gradient = n::grad(objective.mean, {x})[0];
  std::print("Declared selectedresponse {},L2 {},squaredTV {},completeobjective "
             "{},every784gradientfinite {}.\n",
             objective.feature, objective.l2, objective.tv, objective.mean,
             n::all(n::is_finite(gradient)).item<bool>());
  n::save_image_grid(n::concat({first, second}, 0), "build/feature_visualization_noise.png",
                     16, 0, 1, 2, .8, 3);
}
```
